Best 3106 (34%). Missing structure in our versions: the target holds `v1 = &D_800FA878` in a register for the whole body and also keeps `v0 = a0[1]` and `a1 = a0[1]` live across the f14-cursor stores (`sw $v0,0x14($v1)` between `lw $v0,4($a0)` and `sw $v0,0x10($v1)`, similarly `lw $a1,4($a0)` before `addiu v0,a0,8` and `sw $a1,0xc($v1)`). i.e. the original reads each a0 field eagerly and stores the f14 cursor in between — order:
  f8=a0; f14=a0; a3=a0[0]; f14=a0+1; f0=a3; v0=a0[1]; f14=a0+2; f10=v0; a1=a0[1]; f14=a0+3; fc=a1;
